International vocabulary of metrology — JCGM and Inmetro (@ql-source-vim: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_6QKHXBP7KYF6ABT0GXBGYK9BZH
Joint Committee for Guides in Metrology. JCGM 200:2012, International vocabulary of metrology — Basic and general concepts and associated terms, third edition. [Official publication and annotated vocabulary](https://www.bipm.org/en/committees/jc/jcgm/publications) · [Edition DOI](https://doi.org/10.59161/JCGM200-2012).

[Inmetro's VIM 2012, Portuguese PDF](https://www.gov.br/inmetro/pt-br/centrais-de-conteudo/publicacoes/documentos-tecnicos-em-metrologia/vim_2012.pdf) is the luso-Brazilian translation. Begin with chapters 1–2: quantities, values, measurement, measurand, accuracy, precision, error, and uncertainty. Consult chapters 4–5 when reading instrument and calibration claims. The annotated English edition supplies examples and conceptual connections.

Use this as a vocabulary reference while doing calculations, then read the definitions together in the advanced study. A term's familiar everyday meaning can differ from its metrological meaning. Public access does not by itself grant unrestricted adaptation; preserve the JCGM and translation copyright notices and consult their reuse terms. Official edition identities and the Portuguese publication were checked on 28 October 2026. References only; no PDF is bundled.

**Return:** [Quantitative literacy sources — books, standards, and articles](../Sources.lingua#r_7MMXWNA1B4YGA271KMHPPJEK9Q).
} r_6QKHXBP7KYF6ABT0GXBGYK9BZH
